# ====== compose.env (dotenv) template for srv0 ======
# Copy this folder (targets/srv0/config_template/) to config/srv0/ and replace
# every placeholder with a real value, done — no encryption (see AGENTS.md).
# Consumed natively by docker compose via `--env-file config/srv0/compose.env`.
# Quoting: single-quote values containing $ (compose interpolates $ inside
# double quotes). scripts/validate.sh srv0 rejects placeholders and missing keys.

# ====== FRP ======
# The frps (tunnel server) endpoint + its TLS server name.
PROXY_HOST=change_me # the FRPS server hostname/IP
TLS_SERVER_NAME=vps0 # must match the frps server cert CN
# The mTLS certs are REAL FILES at config/srv0/frpc/ (copy them from this
# template folder). Generate the per-pair CA + certs with openssl (once per
# pair, on either machine; save the output directly into config/srv0/frpc/):
#   # CA
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:4096 -keyout ca.key -out ca.crt -days 3650 -nodes -subj "/CN=infra-mtls-ca"
#   # client (srv0)
#   openssl genrsa -out client.key 2048
#   openssl req -new -key client.key -out client.csr -subj "/CN=srv0"
#   openssl x509 -req -in client.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial -out client.crt -days 1825
#   # preboot client (srv0, separate cert for the initramfs frpc)
#   openssl genrsa -out preboot-client.key 2048
#   openssl req -new -key preboot-client.key -out preboot-client.csr -subj "/CN=srv0-preboot"
#   openssl x509 -req -in preboot-client.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial -out preboot-client.crt -days 1825

# ====== Machine facts ======
# MY_UID / DOCKER_GID / USER are NOT in this file — they are machine facts,
# auto-generated into targets/srv0/compose/.env by scripts/prereqs.sh. The
# deploy command passes both files (--env-file config/srv0/compose.env
# --env-file targets/srv0/compose/.env).
